The MIT licence above covers the code in this repository.

It does not cover the Actes uniformes OHADA. Those texts are published by
OHADA and are subject to their own terms; they are not redistributed here.
`data/raw/`, `data/interim/`, `data/processed/`, `data/indexes/` and
`data/training/` are git-ignored and are rebuilt from source with the `kora`
CLI.

Two derived files are committed, and are the project's own work rather than
the corpus:

- `data/eval/gold_qa.jsonl` — 64 hand-written and hand-validated questions with
  short reference answers, quoting only what is necessary to state the expected
  answer.
- `data/corpus_manifest.yaml` — bibliographic metadata for each act: title,
  year, legal status, source URL. No article text.
